{"id":59699,"ord":77,"n_segments":178,"prev":59698,"next":59700,"doc":{"id":"68515","title":"68515_Budd Johnson oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Budd Johnson","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68515/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68515"},"chapter":"Rebuilding the Earl Hines band, 1938-42","title":"Recruiting the new Hines band","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Budd and Billy Eckstine hire Truck Parham, Hurley Ramey, Scoops Cary, trumpeters and trombonists for the new Hines band.","period":"1938","year_from":1938,"year_to":1938,"words":160,"start":[106,0],"end":[107,2],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68515#s59699","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[{"name":"Earl Hines Orchestra","focus":1,"leader":"Earl Hines"}]},"people":[{"name":"Joe MacLewis","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Rabbit","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Harry Jackson","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Jeff","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Ed Simms","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Billy Parkham","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Gil Brockman","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Hurley Ramey","qid":"Q28002497","n":1},{"name":"Truck Parlmheim","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":106,"b":0,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"So meantime I went and me and Billy Parkham went and got Truck Parlmheim."},{"p":106,"b":1,"s":"MR.","x":"Yeah, bass."},{"p":106,"b":2,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Yeah, we got Hurley Ramey."},{"p":106,"b":3,"s":"MR.","x":"Guitar."},{"p":106,"b":4,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And we got Scoops Carry, --"},{"p":106,"b":5,"s":"MR.","x":"Alto sax."},{"p":106,"b":6,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Alto saxophone. We got Gil Brockman, trumpet, we got Ed Simms on trumpet, we got Joe MacLewis on trombone, we had Rapid. I'm going to think of his name in a few minutes."},{"p":106,"b":7,"s":"MR.","x":"Was he the little dark fella?"},{"p":106,"b":8,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Yeah. He was the little --"},{"p":106,"b":9,"s":"MR.","x":"That played trumpet?"},{"p":106,"b":10,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"No, Rabbit was playing trombone."},{"p":106,"b":11,"s":"MR.","x":"Well, who was the little dark fella that played trumpet?"},{"p":106,"b":12,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"That was Harry Jackson, we called him Pee Wee."},{"p":106,"b":13,"s":"MR.","x":"Pee Wee."},{"p":106,"b":14,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"We got him a little bit later."},{"p":106,"b":15,"s":"MR.","x":"I see."},{"p":106,"b":16,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"And we got Joe MacLewis, trombone player. He's from my hometown. And oh, many, we just cooked up a good band. So we had a boy named Jeff -- what was Jeff's last"},{"p":107,"b":0,"s":"MR.","x":"What did he play?"},{"p":107,"b":1,"s":"MR. JOHNSON","x":"Trumpet from Washington. Very fair."},{"p":107,"b":2,"s":"MR.","x":"I can't think of it."}]}